Description: Implements sequential covariate-adjusted randomization (SCR) for
    randomized controlled trials in which participants arrive one at a time.
    SCR separates the covariate imbalance, measured by a modified Mahalanobis
    distance, from the marginal imbalance (the difference in group sizes) and
    minimizes them in a hierarchical order. The package allocates whole
    sequences or single new arrivals, handles continuous and categorical
    covariates, computes imbalance measures, provides a randomization test
    for the treatment effect, and includes a multi-arm extension. See Yang,
    Qin, Li and Hu (2024) <doi:10.1093/biomtc/ujae047>.
